   --- DESCRIPTION KS-1238 ---
The #1034 fix (the connector branch never carries the caller's Bearer) is correct and its 20 cells are green, but the gate identified **four properties the change relies on that no cell pins**. Graded **Minor / test coverage** by the gate, and marked SHIPS-WITH, so it is owed now rather than someday.

## The four unpinned properties

1. **A non-canonical bearer scheme** — e.g. a differently-cased or oddly-spaced `Authorization` value on the connector branch.
2. **The two hand-forwarded fetch routes** — they now send `Authorization: ''` where develop sent the caller's Bearer. Measured on both routes and both trees, but no cell holds it.
3. `platform.ts:254`**.**
4. **A** `rawAuthorization` **fallback for a LIVE caller on a refused exchange.**

## What to do

Add cells for each of the four. They are the properties that would silently regress if someone reworked `authHeaders` or the connector branch, because today nothing reddens.

Related: KS-1215 (the fix), and R-1 (the now-dead `rawAuthorization` capture).

---

Filed from the #1034 / KS-1215 tier-1 gate report `2026-09-18-ks1215-1034-e4624218b-tier1-r1`, at merge of `a105cd32b1ed9c6927ae6e797f8259224d8480c6`. Pre-existing unless stated; **not** introduced by #1034.
   --- END ---
   --- COMMENT 77f4ec90-d30c-4185-a8f6-815b2924d57e 2026-09-19T16:37:27.931Z ---
#1095 and #1096 are merged: test files only, zero product bytes. The batch gate (2026-09-20-batch1092-1096-tier1-r1) graded KS-1238 NOT-COMPLETE, so the ticket goes back to Backlog. Every item listed after #1091 is now pinned, each measured over the whole api-gateway suite: the anchoring-verify forward verification.ts:597-598 by #1095 (RAW598 reds exactly its found-document cell, 1 of 648 at its head and 1 of 654 with all five merged, 0 of 646 before); POST /api/documents at verification.ts:1297 by #1095 (RAW1297 reds exactly its create cell, 1 of 648 and 1 of 654, 0 of 646 before); (iii) the F-1 super-admin cell for the kept platform.ts:254 by #1096 (the refresh-tenants Authorization dropped reds exactly that cell, 1 of 649 and 1 of 654, 0 of 646 before; a raw-header swap there reds 0 of 654 because every caller that reaches :254 has raw equal to the post-auth header, and every connector is refused 403 at :239, whose removal reds 1); (iv) the register-connector cell with a LIVE JWT on a REFUSED exchange by #1096 (a LIVE-only fallback in the handler reds exactly that cell, 1 of 649 and 1 of 654, 0 of 646 before; the auth-layer fallback reds 15). (i), (ii), :516 and :521 stay pinned. Still open, measured with all five merged (654 cells): POST /api/users/admin/create and PATCH /api/users/admin/:id in routes/proxy.ts (:472 / :504, authenticateToken(true), hand-forwarding the Authorization at :475 / :507) are unreachable only because routes/admin.ts registers the same two paths first; renaming either admin.ts path reds 0 of 654, and with a path unshadowed plus a raw read at :475 or :507 a revoked session's Bearer reaches the upstream (in-process). One cell per path pinning that a connector key alone gets 401 there closes it. KS-1280 is outside this ticket.
